-- H2. a column added after the part was written, so the part records no type for it
H2 column not stored	1
H2 authoritative	1073741824	4
H2 with projections	1073741824	4
-- N. the price of refusing when the part records no type: the answer is right, the
--    projection is skipped until a merge rewrites the part
N answer	1073741825	4
N after merge	1073741825	6
-- J. the same price for a type change that happens to keep every value: the projection is
--    skipped although its stored keys are still right. This is deliberate: whether the
--    stored values survived a conversion cannot be decided without recomputing them, and
--    the previous case shows how rewriting the part brings the projection back
J authoritative	1073741825	1
J authoritative	1073741827	1
J authoritative	1073741829	1
J authoritative	1073741831	1
J with projections	1073741825	1
J with projections	1073741827	1
J with projections	1073741829	1
J with projections	1073741831	1
-- Q. an intermediate of a DEFAULT chain that the part does not record cannot be shown NOT to
--    be staleness, so it is refused even with nothing retyped: the projection froze a value
--    computed through that intermediate under a declaration no part recorded. This is the
--    price arms N and J price, and rewriting the part brings the projection back the way
--    arm N shows
Q neither d nor c stored by the part	1
Q authoritative	1073741824	4
